{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1192966-breaking-points-question","id":1192966,"title":"Breaking points Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-07T22:04:18-08:00","id":1192966,"title":"Breaking points Question","content":"Can an Uratha fail a breaking point roll voluntarily ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T22:29:22-08:00","id":1192974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1192966-breaking-points-question#post1192966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can an Uratha fail a breaking point roll voluntarily ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would make this a ST preference. I don't allow for voluntary Breaking Points because of the way Harmony works, but your ST might","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T22:43:04-08:00","id":1192977,"title":"","content":"Because Harmony is a balance rather than a scale, no. You can get benefits from failing a breaking point as a werewolf rather than a vampire for example as it only gets worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T07:09:54-08:00","id":1193094,"title":"","content":"This is an interesting question because I don't see anything in the rules that say you can't. It is actually pretty easy to sabotage your own Harmony by creating easily disposed of Touchstones. Losing a Touchstone is a automatic Harmony adjustment, no breaking point roll needed. <br /> <br /> <br /> So I think I will err on the side of allowing voluntary breaking point fail, but I would want something in return, I would require the player take a Condition of my choice that he has to deal with for the rest of the Chapter (or longer). That will encourage some role-playing of the paradigm shift of a Harmony change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T16:36:00-08:00","id":1193353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1192966-breaking-points-question?p=1193094#post1193094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an interesting question because I don't see anything in the rules that say you can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also nothing in the rules that says you <i>can</i> voluntarily fail any kind of roll, Harmony or otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T21:35:48-08:00","id":1193427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1192966-breaking-points-question?p=1193353#post1193353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also nothing in the rules that says you <i>can</i> voluntarily fail any kind of roll, Harmony or otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well this is what I get for posting while coffee free. You can choose to dramatically fail a failure (that;s what I was thinking of), but you still have to roll the failure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T09:02:14-08:00","id":1193581,"title":"","content":"In fact, in the Demon sub-forum it was once discussed and the Dev specifically said you shouldn't allow intentionally failing an Embed roll to get its failure effect. He went on to point out that if you want to actively do a thing, then you should make a new power that actively rolls for what you do want to do. I stand by that for all things in ChroD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}